obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000097 \"A cell that is found in almost all tissues containing numerous basophilic granules and capable of releasing large amounts of histamine and heparin upon activation. Progenitors leave bone marrow and mature in connective and mucosal tissue. Mature mast cells are found in all tissues, except the bloodstream. Their phenotype is CD117-high, CD123-negative, CD193-positive, CD200R3-positive, and FceRI-high. Stem-cell factor (KIT-ligand; SCF) is the main controlling signal of their survival and development.\")\n\n  Line 4749: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:068340007X\") oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_0000097 \"tissue basophil\")\n\n  Line 4875: AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000233 obo:CL_0000111 <https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/1069>)\n\n  Line 4912: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"MESH:D042783\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:21275341\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Endothelial_cell\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://sourceforge.net/tracker/?func=detail&atid=440764&aid=3364936&group_id=36855\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000115 \"An endothelial cell comprises the outermost layer or lining of anatomical structures and can be squamous or cuboidal. In mammals, endothelial cell has vimentin filaments and is derived from the mesoderm.\")\n\n  Line 5001: AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000233 obo:CL_0000124 <https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/715>)\n\n  Line 5014: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0000125 \"Not all glial cells develop from glioblasts, with microglia developing from the mesoderm instead. See https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/1571\")\n\n  Line 5090: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:21976958\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:23284695\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"