at-storing cell found mostly in the abdominal cavity and subcutaneous tissue of mammals. Fat is usually stored in the form of triglycerides.\")\n\n  Line 5172: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GO_REF:0000034\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"MESH:D019902\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32491508\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000138 \"A skeletogenic cell that secretes a specialized, avascular, GAG-rich matrix, is embedded in cartilage tissue matrix, retains the ability to divide, and develops from a chondroblast cell.\")\n\n  Line 5193: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GO_REF:0000034\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000140 \"Skeletogenic cell that secretes dentine matrix, is derived from odontogenic papilla. Embedded in dentine tissue, and is the transformation of a non-terminally differentiated odontoblast cell.\")\n\n  Line 5376: AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000233 obo:CL_0000161 <https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/427>)\n\n  Line 5579: AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000233 obo:CL_0000181 <https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/720>)\n\n  Line 5836: AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000233 obo:CL_0000212 <https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/2271>)\n\n  Line 5843: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"JB:jb\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000213 \"OBSOLETE. A cell within an epithelial cell sheet whose main function is to act as an internal or external covering for a tissue or an organism.\")\n\n  Line 5844: AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000233 obo:CL_0000213 <https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/3014>)\n\n  Line 5862: AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000233 obo:CL_0000215 <https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/3012>)\n\n  Line 5882: AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000233 obo:CL_0000217 <https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/3013>)\n\n  Line 6047: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GO_REF:0000031\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:16213494\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:1919437\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000235 \"A mononuclear phagocyte present in variety of tissues, typically differentiated from monocytes, capable of phagocytosing a variety of extracellular particulate material, including immune complexes, microorganisms, and dead cells.\")\n\n  Line 6054: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0000235 \"Morphology: Diameter 30_M-80 _M, abundant cytoplasm, low N/C ratio, eccentric nucleus. Irregular shape with pseudopods, highly adhesive. Contain vacuoles and phagosomes, may contain azurophilic granules; markers: Mouse & Human: CD68, in most cases CD11b. Mouse: in most cases F4/80+; role or process: immune, antigen presentation, & tissue remodelling; lineage: hematopoietic, myeloid.\")\n\n  Line 6128: AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000233 obo:CL_0000243 <https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/715>)\n\n  Line 6286: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0471245208\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000266 \"Obsolete. Use PO:0004011 from Plant Ontology instead. A cell constituting an active locus of meristematic activity in a tissue composed of somewhat older, differentiating cells.\")\n\n  Line 6299: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0471245208\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000268 \"Obsolete. Consult Plant Ontology instead. The cell in the phloem tissue concerned with mainly longitudinal conduction of food materials. Classified into sieve cell and sieve tube member.\")\n\n  Line 6311: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:047124520\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000270 \"Obsolete. Use PO:0000284 from Plant Ontology instead. An epidermal cell associated with a stoma and at least morphologically distinguishable from the epidermal cells composing the groundmass of the tissue.\")\n\n  Line 6441: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0471245208\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000290 \"Obsolete. Use PO:0000274 from Plant Ontology instead. A fiber of the xylem tissue, Two types are recognized in the secondary xylem: fiber tracheids and libriform fibers.\")\n\n  Line 6463: AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000233 obo:CL_0000293 <https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/3010>)\n\n  Line 6595: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:15749908\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:19256306\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:19727116\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:29713660\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37873034\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000312 \"An epithelial cell of stratified squamous tissues, including skin, oral mucosa (Hiroshima et al., 2011), and esophagus (Whelan et al., 2018), that produces keratin proteins and secretes antimicrobial peptides to form a resilient barrier against environmental damage, dehydration, pathogens, and microbial invasion. It undergoes successive stages of differentiation marked by changes in keratin expression, supporting tissue integrity, wound repair, and contributing to immune defense.\")\n\n  Line 6668: AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000233 obo:CL_0000321 <https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/1149>)\n\n  Line 6723: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0000328 \"see: https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/161\")\n\n  Line 6995: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0471245208\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000364 \"Obsolete. Consult Plant Ontology. A cell that develops from the ray initial and composes all rays (panels of tissue variable in height and width, formed by the ray initials in the vascular cambium and extending radially in the secondary xylem and secondary phloem) in the secondary vascular tissues.\")\n\n  Line 7117: AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000233 obo:CL_0000381 <https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/1784>)\n\n  Line 7151: AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000233 obo:CL_0000386 <https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/3016>)\n\n  Line 7186: AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000233 obo:CL_0000391 <https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/1949>)\n\n  Line 7207: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://doi.org/10.1016/B978-012369493-5.50008-0\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000394 \"A phagocytic hemocyte, responsible for the engulfment of small particles, microbes, and apoptotic tissue debris. It may also secretes antimicrobial peptides and contribute to the production and secretion of proteins of the hemolymph.\")\n\n  Line 7233: AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000233 obo:CL_0000398 <https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/1949>)\n\n  Line 7254: AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000233 obo:CL_0000401 <https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/1949>)\n\n  Line 7263: AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000233 obo:CL_0000402 <https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/2869>)\n\n  Line 7283: AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000233 obo:CL_0000405 <https://github.com/FlyBase/drosophila-anatomy-developmental-ontology/issues/1621>)\n\n  Line 7431: AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000233 obo:CL_0000426 <https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/708>)\n\n  Line 7432: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0000426 \"This is a cell used in tissue engineering and is out of scope for CL.\")\n\n  Line 7475: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0517223651\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Reticular_cell\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000432 \"A fibroblast that synthesizes collagen and uses it to produce reticular fibers, thus providing structural support. Reticular cells are found in many organs, including the spleen, lymph nodes and kidneys. Subtypes of reticular cells include epithelial, mesenchymal, and fibroblastic reticular cells. Fibroblastic reticular cells are involved in directing B cells and T cells to specific regions within a tissue, whereas epithelial and mesenchymal reticular cells are associated with certain areas of the brain.\")\n\n  Line 7479: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso obo:CL_0000432 \"https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/1472\")\n\n  Line 7550: SubClassOf(Annotation(obo:IAO_0000233 \"https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/1943\") obo:CL_0000441 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002162 obo:NCBITaxon_6656))\n\n  Line 7554: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:127520252\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000442 \"A cell with extensive dendritic processes found in the B cell areas (primary follicles and germinal centers) of lymphoid tissue. They are unrelated to the dendritic cell associated with T cells. Follicular dendritic cells have Fc receptors and C3b receptors, but unlike other dendritic cells, they do not process or present antigen in a way that allows recognition by T cells. Instead, they hold antigen in the form of immune complexes on their surfaces for long periods and can present antigen to B cells during an immune response.\")\n\n  Line 7613: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"MESH:D002001\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000449 \"A cell from the thermogenic form of adipose tissue found in many species,  particularly in newborns and hibernating mammals, but also in lesser amounts in adults of other mammals including humans. Brown fat is capable of rapid liberation of energy and seems to be important in the maintenance of body temperature immediately after birth and upon waking from hibernation.\")\n\n  Line 7631: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0781735149\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000451 \"A cell of hematopoietic origin, typically resident in particular tissues, specialized in the uptake, processing, and transport of antigens to lymph nodes for the purpose of stimulating an immune response via T cell activation. These cells are lineage negative (CD3-negative, CD19-negative, CD34-negative, and CD56-negative).\")\n\n  Line 7646: AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000233 obo:CL_0000452 <https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/3161>)\n\n  Line 7799: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0471245208\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000472 \"Obsolete. Use PO:0000076 from Plant Ontology instead. OBSOLETE, use term from Plant Ontology. Parenchyma cells containing chloroplasts; a component of leaf mesophyll and other green parenchyma tissue.\")\n\n  Line 7847: SubClassOf(Annotation(oboInOwl:source <https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/589>) obo:CL_0000477 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002162 obo:NCBITaxon_50557))\n\n  Line 7886: # Class: obo:CL_0000484 (connective tissue type mast cell)\n\n  Line 7888: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:dsd\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:19923473\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:9354811\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000484 \"Mast cell subtype whose granules contain both the serine proteases tryptase and chymase. These cells are primarily found in connective tissue, such as the peritoneal cavity, skin, and intestinal submucosa. Their development is T-cell independent.\")\n\n  Line 7893: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0000484 \"connective tissue type mast cell\")\n\n  Line 7899: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:dsd\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:19923473\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:9354811\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000485 \"Mast cell subtype that contains only the serine protease trypase in its granules. These cells are primarily found in mucosal tissue, such as intestinal mucosa and alveoli. They depend upon T-cells for development of phenotype.\")\n\n  Line 8006: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"MESH:D017154\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000499 \"A connective tissue cell of an organ found in the loose connective tissue.\")\n\n  Line 8224: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso obo:CL_0000525 \"https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/2100\")\n\n  Line 8324: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0471245208\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000539 \"OBSOLETE: A cell in a tissue that markedly differs in form, size, or contents from other cells in the same tissue.\")\n\n  Line 8330: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"MESH:D009474\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Neuron\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000540 \"The basic cellular unit of nervous tissue. Each neuron consists of a body, an axon, and dendrites. Their purpose is to receive, conduct, and transmit impulses in the nervous system.\")\n\n  Line 8437: AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000233 obo:CL_0000548 <https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/2124>)\n\n  Line 8738: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GO_REF:0000031\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"MESH:D009000\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000576 \"Myeloid mononuclear recirculating leukocyte that can act as a precursor of tissue macrophages, osteoclasts and some populations of tissue dendritic cells.\")\n\n  Line 8742: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0000576 \"Morphology: Mononuclear cell, diameter, 14 to 20 _M, N/C ratio 2:1-1:1. Nucleus may appear in variety of shapes: round, kidney, lobulated, or convoluted. Fine azurophilic granules present; markers: CD11b (shared with other myeloid cells), human: CD14, mouse: F4/80-mid,GR1-low; location: Blood, but can be recruited into tissues; role or process: immune & tissue remodelling; lineage: hematopoietic, myeloid.\")\n\n  Line 8815: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:ana\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:dsd\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GO_REF:0000031\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"MESH:D016676\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000583 \"A tissue-resident macrophage found in the alveoli of the lungs. Ingests small inhaled particles resulting in degradation and presentation of the antigen to immunocompetent cells. Markers include F4/80-positive, CD11b-/low, CD11c-positive, CD68-positive, sialoadhesin-positive, dectin-1-positive, MR-positive, CX3CR1-negative.\")\n\n  Line 9215: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"TAIR:sr\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000627 \"OBSOLETE. A cell involved in transporting nutrients, minerals, water, gases and other chemicals between cells for a variety of purposes including conveying nutrition to other tissues, removing waste products from the tissues, conveying gases for respiration, distributing heat and repelling invasion of foreign substances.\")\n\n  Line 9216: AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000233 obo:CL_0000627 <https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/2990>)\n\n  Line 9386: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0412046911\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0517223651\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31915267\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pituicyte\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000645 \"A glial cell of astrocytic lineage with long processes running parallel to adjacent axons in the proximal infundibulum of the neurohypophysis. These processes form a three-dimensional network among the axons of the hypothalamic neurosecretory cells and are connected by gap junctions which provide for their metabolic coupling. This cell type constitutes most of the nonexcitable tissue in the neurohypophsis; function may include possibly acting as an intermediate in the modulation of oxytocin and vasopressin release. This cell type is highly variable in size and shape and commonly contain lipid droplets and deposits of lipochrome pigment.\")\n\n  Line 9487: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso obo:CL_0000653 \"https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/1460\")\n\n  Line 9564: AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000233 obo:CL_0000663 <https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/726>)\n\n  Line 9571: AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000233 obo:CL_0000664 <https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/726>)\n\n  Line 9578: AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000233 obo:CL_0000665 <https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/726>)\n\n  Line 9585: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"DOI:10.1007/978-3-211-99390-3_133\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000666 \"An endothelial cell that has small pores, or fenestrations, which allow for the efficient exchange of substances between the blood and surrounding tissues.\")\n\n  Line 9599: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0471245208\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000668 \"OBSOLETE: The cell characteristic of an organ, as distinguished from associated connective or supporting tissues.\")\n\n  Line 10004: AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000233 obo:CL_0000717 <https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/1364>)\n\n  Line 10071: AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000233 obo:CL_0000727 <https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/1930>)\n\n  Line 10078: AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000233 obo:CL_0000728 <https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/1930>)\n\n  Line 10085: AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000233 obo:CL_0000729 <https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/1930>)\n\n  Line 10149: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:978-0-323-05290-0\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000738 \"An achromatic cell of the myeloid or lymphoid lineages capable of ameboid movement, found in blood or other tissue.\")\n\n\n(Results truncated: showing 100 of 314 matches (214 hidden). Consider using a more specific 